        "original_id": "3b38c09c-474e-5c7b-9426-e6a5fbbbded8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Edward Burne-Jones, William Morris\n- Artworks: The Beguiling of Merlin, Pygmalion and the Image, Pygmalion and Galatea series\n- Organizations: Morris, Marshall, Faulkner & Co.\n- Roles: Pre-Raphaelite painter, artist, designer, founding partner\n- Topics: Pre-Raphaelite movement, decorative arts\n\nFacts:\n- Edward Burne-Jones was born on 28 August 1833 and died on 17 June 1898.\n- Edward Burne-Jones was a British artist and designer associated with the later phase of the Pre-Raphaelite movement.\n- Edward Burne-Jones worked closely with William Morris on a wide range of decorative arts.\n- Edward Burne-Jones was a founding partner in Morris, Marshall, Faulkner & Co.\n- The Beguiling of Merlin is a painting by the Pre-Raphaelite painter Edward Burne-Jones that was created between 1872 and 1877.\n- Pygmalion and the Image is the second series of four oil paintings in the Pygmalion and Galatea series by Edward Burne-Jones, completed between 1875 and 1878.",
